      "knowledge_point_id": "66c5a147-0100-5f4b-a221-25b8674b2115",
      "knowledge_point": "Evaluating the Integral of a Sum of Two Functions",
      "problem": "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{4}(2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}(2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{4}(2{x}^{3/2}+3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we split the integral into the difference of three integrals and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}(2{x}^{3/2}+3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{4}{x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x+3{\\int }_{0}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{4}1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}{x}^{5/2}{|}_{0}^{4}+3\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{4}+x\\,{|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}{x}^{5/2}{|}_{0}^{4}+\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{4}+x\\,{|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}({4}^{5/2}-{0}^{5/2})+\\frac{3}{2}({4}^{2}-{0}^{2})+(4-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot 32+\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 16+4 \\\\  & =\\frac{128}{5}+28 \\\\  & =\\frac{268}{5}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
